  "source": "Elspec, EQ-ACR (EQ-Activar) 3-Phase Balanced System User Manual V22, document SMX-0609-0101, January 2026, section Native Serial Modbus (tables 12 to 14)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "EQ-ACR 3 Phase Balanced System User Manual (EQ- Activar, V22)",
      "version": "V22, SMX-0609-0101, January 2026",
      "url": "https://www.elspec-ltd.com/download/eq-acr-3-phase-balanced-system-user-manual/",
      "note": "Native serial Modbus chapter: status and control variables, status bits and parameter addresses (tables 12 to 14).",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "333084d10a5eef074eb2628c8ba3b5e3980940e98fd5997938c1f1e48272b2ab"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Read-only native serial Modbus RTU: 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit; the baud rate is detected automatically between 9600 and 115200 bps and the slave ID (1 to 32) is set from the front panel.",
    "The manual says all parameters are 4x registers, read with function 3 (offset 40000) or function 4 (offset 30000). They are listed here as holding registers (function 3). Addresses are the PLC addresses of the manual, address base 1 (subtract 1 for the wire address); hexadecimal addresses are written as printed.",
    "All values are IEEE 754 single-precision floats in real units (volts, amperes) in the standard Modbus byte order; the manual says the byte order may have to be changed in some applications, so big-endian is assumed. The system status register is a 16-bit value.",
    "Names are decoded from the manual's identifiers (r, s, t = L1, L2, L3; rs, st, tr = L12, L23, L31; 1 = mains, 2 = capacitor system, 3 = load centre); the manual's own identifier is in each description. Units are only given where the manual states them (volts, amperes, kW and kVAr for the 15-minute and monthly values); the manual gives none for the power, power factor and THD values.",
    "Only the first harmonic of each series is listed (the manual lists VrH1 to It3H1); the following harmonics are at consecutive addresses in steps of 2, e.g. the 2nd harmonic of VrH1 is at 0x0303. The number of harmonics is not stated. The Fault parameter (0x2101) is left out because its format is not stated. The 15-minute and monthly table is available from firmware 4.0.3 or 5.0.3.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 1,
  "x_status": "official",
